Description: JOG SENSITIVITY setting in the on-screen settings menu
 How hard a nudge of the jog side ring pushes the track is a matter of
 taste and of the wheel in front of you, and until now it was a constant
 compiled into the build: the DDJ-400 mapping's bendScale, which cannot be
 reached from the touchscreen at all.
 .
 This adds it to the settings menu as its own page. MINUS and PLUS step the
 sensitivity in 10-point increments between 20% and 200% of the built-in
 feel, and each step takes effect on the decks immediately -- a feel setting
 is only ever judged by putting a hand on the wheel, so the page would be
 useless if it needed a commit before it could be tried.
 .
 SAVE is what makes the value outlast the session. It writes mixxx.cfg and
 flushes it to disk there and then, rather than leaving it to the save Mixxx
 does on a clean exit: POWER OFF is two rows up in this same menu and cuts
 the power from under the process, so a setting that only survived a tidy
 shutdown would not survive the way this unit is actually turned off. The
 button shows SAVE while the value differs from the one on disk and an inert
 SAVED once they match, so there is never any doubt about what a reboot will
 bring back. Leaving the page without saving keeps the new feel for the rest
 of the session and offers SAVE again when the page is reopened.
 .
 The value lives in RateControl, next to the nudge calculation that consumes
 it, as a single setting shared by every deck (the shape the rate-ramp
 settings already use). Applying it there rather than in the controller
 mapping means it holds for any controller, any mapping and the keyboard,
 and cannot be shadowed by a stale copy of the DDJ-400 script in the user's
 own controller directory. Every RateControl loads it from mixxx.cfg in its
 constructor, so the saved feel is in force from the first audio buffer,
 before the skin or the library exist.
 .
 Only the playing deck's nudge is scaled. The same jog factor scrubs a
 paused deck, and cueing should not get faster or slower because the
 beatmatch nudge was tuned.
 .
 Skin side (jog.xml, settings.xml, style.qss in the Pioneered theme): the
 page is a centred panel fenced in by the settings menu's own scrim, and it
 is raised and cleared through the same menu_subpage mechanism as the Wi-Fi
 and software update pages.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

